# The program writes one closure and hands it over at every turn of the loop, and the helper can tell: it keeps what it is handed. A cell made anew on the failing side of each turn would be another object each time.
# So only a closure that the block of the call itself makes goes to the failing side.
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK: = NewClosure
# CHECK: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-NOT: = NewClosure
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: 36 1
